---
description: No em dashes in agent writing. No en dashes used as clause breaks. Hyphens in compound words are fine.
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Em Dashes

- Do not use em dashes (U+2014) in chat, progress updates, documentation, comments, commit messages, or other generated writing.
- Do not use an en dash (U+2013) to separate clauses, set off an aside, or break a sentence. En dashes are only for numeric or date ranges.
- Use a comma, parentheses, a colon, a semicolon, or a new sentence. Hyphens in compounds (`well-known`, `user-defined`) are fine.
- Before sending or saving, replace any em dash or sentence-break en dash.

Example: "The update is ready, pending review."
